    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "idk, the \"human element\" sounds great for a textbook but in the real world, businesses fail if they aren't lean. if i keep people around just for \"loyalty\" while my competitors use ai to slash their margins and undercut my prices, im basically killing the company. isnt it more \"socially responsible\" to keep the company profitable and stable by using the most efficient tools available?",
